The notable real finding this run surfaced: the implementation's "latest background check per type" selection was tie-breaking on `created_at` alone, which collapses under the test harness's pinned clock — so a re-screening flag was being silently ignored and a volunteer wrongly stayed `ELIGIBLE` instead of `SCREENING_FAILED`. Fixed by adding the monotonic insertion sequence as the tie-break. Every step's verbatim subagent summary is recorded in `worklog.md`.
